{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he did not know anything with him.</b> Joseph did not take counsel with him concerning anything but the delicacies of his table, as it says, ״כי אם הלחם אשר הוא אוכל״ — save the bread that he ate. And furthermore, the term 'bread' (לחם) may include an allusion to his wife, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 2:20): ״קראן לו ויאכל לחם״ — 'they called him and he ate bread.' And it is written (Proverbs 30:20): ״אכלה ומחתה פיה״ — 'she ate and wiped her mouth.' And so he explains further on: ״כי אם אותך באשר את אשתו״ — 'save you, in that you are his wife.'" "<b>And Joseph was beautiful of form and beautiful of appearance.</b> Scripture reveals to us his beauty, on account of which his mistress sought him. And it says:"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:50.042272934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}